<parameter name="path">/root/api-design-prototype/prototype/README.md</parameter>
<parameter name="content"># API Design Prototype

A production-ready API prototype demonstrating REST API design best practices.

## Features

- ✅ JWT-based authentication
- ✅ Role-based access control (admin/user)
- ✅ Input validation with Joi
- ✅ Rate limiting
- ✅ Request/response standardization
- ✅ Pagination with filtering and sorting
- ✅ Comprehensive error handling
- ✅ CORS and security headers (Helmet)
- ✅ Health check endpoints
- ✅ In-memory data store (easily replacable with real database)

## Quick Start

### Installation

```bash
cd prototype
npm install
cp .env.example .env
npm start
```

### Development mode with auto-restart

```bash
npm run dev
```

## API Endpoints

### Health Check
- `GET /health` - Basic health check
- `GET /health/detailed` - Detailed system info

### Authentication
- `POST /api/v1/auth/register` - Register new user
- `POST /api/v1/auth/login` - Login user
- `GET /api/v1/auth/me` - Get current user

### Users
- `GET /api/v1/users` - List all users (authenticated)
- `GET /api/v1/users/me` - Get current user details
- `PATCH /api/v1/users/me` - Update current user
- `DELETE /api/v1/users/me` - Delete current user
- `GET /api/v1/users/:id` - Get user by ID

### Tasks
- `GET /api/v1/tasks` - List tasks (with pagination, filtering, sorting)
- `GET /api/v1/tasks/:id` - Get specific task
- `POST /api/v1/tasks` - Create new task (authenticated)
- `PATCH /api/v1/tasks/:id` - Update task (owner or admin)
- `DELETE /api/v1/tasks/:id` - Delete task (owner or admin)

## Query Parameters

### Pagination
- `page` - Page number (default: 1)
- `per_page` - Items per page (default: 20, max: 100)

### Task Filtering
- `status` - Filter by status: `pending`, `in_progress`, `completed`, `cancelled`
- `priority` - Filter by priority: `low`, `medium`, `high`, `urgent`
- `q` - Search by title or description
- `sort` - Sort by field, use `-` prefix for descending (e.g., `-created_at`)

### User Filtering
- `role` - Filter by role: `admin`, `user`
- `q` - Search by name or email

## Request Examples

### Register
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/register \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "email": "test@example.com",
    "password": "SecurePass123",
    "name": "Test User"
  }'
```

### Login
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/login \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "email": "test@example.com",
    "password": "SecurePass123"
  }'
```

### Create Task
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/tasks \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" \
  -d '{
    "title": "New Task",
    "description": "Task description",
    "priority": "high"
  }'
```

### Get Tasks with Filters
```bash
curl "http://localhost:3000/api/v1/tasks?status=pending&priority=high&sort=-created_at&page=1&per_page=10" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN"
```

## Response Format

### Success Response
```json
{
  "data": { ... }
}
```

### Paginated Response
```json
{
  "data": [...],
  "pagination": {
    "page": 1,
    "per_page": 20,
    "total": 50,
    "total_pages": 3,
    "has_next": true,
    "has_prev": false
  },
  "links": {
    "self": "?page=1&per_page=20",
    "first": "?page=1&per_page=20",
    "last": "?page=3&per_page=20",
    "next": "?page=2&per_page=20"
  }
}
```

### Error Response
```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
    "message": "The request failed validation",
    "details": [
      {
        "field": "email",
        "message": "Invalid email format"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

## Project Structure

```
prototype/
├── src/
│   ├── server.js              # Application entry point
│   ├── config/                # Configuration
│   ├── routes/                # Route handlers
│   │   ├── auth.js            # Authentication routes
│   │   ├── users.js           # User routes
│   │   ├── tasks.js           # Task routes
│   │   ├── health.js          # Health check routes
│   │   └── index.js           # Route aggregator
│   ├── middleware/            # Express middleware
│   │   ├── authenticate.js    # JWT authentication
│   │   ├── validateRequest.js # Request validation
│   │   ├── rateLimiter.js     # Rate limiting
│   │   └── errorHandler.js    # Error handling
│   ├── models/                # Data models
│   │   ├── database.js        # In-memory database
│   │   ├── User.js            # User model
│   │   └── Task.js            # Task model
│   └── utils/                 # Utilities
│       ├── errors.js          # Custom error classes
│       └── helpers.js         # Helper functions
├── package.json
├── .env.example
└── README.md
```

## Default Users

The system initializes with two default users:

| Email | Password | Role |
|-------|----------|------|
| admin@example.com | admin123 | admin |
| user@example.com | user123 | user |

## Environment Variables

| Variable | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| PORT | 3000 | Server port |
| NODE_ENV | development | Environment mode |
| JWT_SECRET | - | JWT signing secret |
| JWT_EXPIRES_IN | 1h | JWT expiration time |
| RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS | 900000 | Rate limit window (15 min) |
| RATE_LIMIT_MAX | 100 | Max requests per window |

## Security Features

- Helmet.js for security headers
- CORS configuration
- Rate limiting per IP/user
- JWT authentication
- Password hashing with bcrypt
- Input validation and sanitization
- Error handling without stack traces in production
</parameter>
